;; wai's validator (doc/wasm/WAI.md §7; doc/wasm/WASM-SURVEY.md WAS30 (a), WA5): a module's binary checked by Wasm 3.0's typing
;; rules before wai decodes it, on its own (the decoder assumes a valid module). Written after the specification's validation
;; algorithm (its appendix: an operand stack whose unreachable code has an unknown bottom, a control stack of frames, the
;; locals' initialization) and valid.ml's rules at wg-3.0, as arbace.wasm.valid (WA3) states them; judged against
;; arbace.wasm.valid's verdicts over the testsuite's modules (the `valid/` rows beside the eval cell). Its types are the
;; decoder's canonical ones (iso-recursive equivalence as id equality); an unknown type is K 0, an unknown heap type hBot.


